A||N||3||BobC||Anyone know of a reasonably low miles '88 5 spd Formula or GT for sale?||||6
Z||000000||BobC||11-02-1999||10:17 PM||||I've sorta settled on the '88's due to the better suspension and brakes.  I want a 5 spd, because I love driving a stick.  I need AC.  I want the V6 so I don't need to feel inferior.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I like cruise, but its not critical.  Same with power windows and locks, but I'm silly to want them on a 12 yr old car, I know.  I plan to drive the car, for the most part, not show it.<P>I like the Yellow best, but they seem really pricey compared to the other colors.  I found a Formula with 26k for $7300 and another with 69k for $6900. So they are basically $2000-$2500 over retail book, at least.  <P>I also like the Black, Gold and Silver.  I'm not really liking the Red's or White, I guess.  <P>How hard (as in how much) for a good repaint?  A super-yellow (like the Y2k Vette) would be a good color to do if I was buying something and then getting it painted.<P>Mileage wise, I'd like to find something thats been driven and well maintained, not just stored, so anything under 100k miles is Ok.<P>I talked to a person today.  She has a Black '88 GT with over 100k.  The problem is that someone told her she can get $4000 to $5000 for it.  Its sort of sad, because she loves the car, but it can't be a only car daily driver for her.  I maybe could see spending $3000 for it, which of course wouldn't make her happy.  I'll likely end up in the same boat if and when I ever sell my T/A.<P>Know of something nice and not overly pricey?  Email me or post it here, please.<P>BobC||||reg||6
Z||000001||88 Database Nut||11-03-1999||08:36 AM||||Hey BobC, goto autotrader.com or classifieds2000.com and do a search on 1988 only fieros.  I go there alot to search for VINs for my '88 Fiero Database project (836 cars and counting), and there are literally<BR>hundreds of cars for sale there, all around the US.  Another good place to look is cars.com, and the forsale section of the Minnessoooota Fiero club (sorry, don't know the URL off the top of my head).  There's lots of other places, if you can't find what you want there, let me know and I'll point you to more.<P>Good Luck, Hold out for what you want, you're bound to find a bargain if you keep looking.||||reg||6
Z||000002||Standard||11-04-1999||12:00 AM||||The url for Minnesota Fieros Forever is <A HREF="http://www.fiero.mn.org" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.mn.org</A> <P>It's gotten alot better since I first visited the site.. I'd like to join but I have to work mondays so I couldn't get to the meetings.. grrr||||reg||14
Z||000003||BobC||11-12-1999||09:49 PM||||Well, I've been looking a while and hadn't found anything both reasonably close by and priced for something with not too many miles and in real good shape.<P>In my web travels looking I happened upon a car with a 3.4L DOHC and the Getrag Hi Perf 5 spd.  Its a 91 Grand Prix with 70k miles and all the toys.  Clutch, battery, tires and timing belt are all recently replaced.  I don't suppose many of them were made, but it isn't a big issue for me, its rarity.  Price was under $5k and it was well taken care of.<BR>Maybe someday I'll look at a Fiero, again.  Till then, happy trails, and thanks for the help looking...<P> <A HREF="http://people.ce.mediaone.net/bcurrey/temp/gpse91briteblu.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://people.ce.mediaone.net/bcurrey/temp/gpse91briteblu.jpg</A> ||||reg||6
